# WolkaraForever layer patch 0065 - Battery Saver: presentation pacing and the AFK dim
#
# Why: the launcher's Battery Saver submenu stores a frame limit and an AFK timeout, and
# something has to enforce them. Both are applied at boundaries the adapters already own:
# the guest's own presentation call, and the host view that receives every input.
#
# Metal. Apple documents three kinds of presentation on a command buffer - immediate, timed
# and minimum-duration, the last of which "holds the previous drawable for at least the
# specified duration" (MTLCommandBuffer). A cap is therefore expressible in the guest's own
# calls, which is why there is no second swizzle and no separate render loop here:
#
#   immediate          -> presentDrawable:afterMinimumDuration: with the cap's interval
#   minimum-duration   -> the guest's duration, or the cap's, whichever is longer
#   timed (atTime:)    -> the guest's time, or no-earlier-than the previous frame for this
#                         layer plus the interval, whichever is later
#
# With the cap Off nothing is installed at all: the presentation path is the one it had
# before this feature existed. The environment - charger, Low Power Mode, thermal state - is
# re-resolved at most once a second on the render path, and the AFK dim's 10 FPS applies
# immediately through its notification.
#
# Two accuracy fixes come with it. The simulator SDK has no presented timestamp, and the
# acquisition time was being fed to AKRecordMetalFramePresented as if it were one: that
# labelled the drawable acquisition rate as presented FPS, which is the number the HUD must
# not invent. It is no longer recorded, so the published rates stay 0 and the HUD says it has
# no measurement. On the runtime without minimum-duration presentation (the simulator's
# Metal does not implement it; the device's does) the immediate path falls back to timed
# presentation with the same no-earlier-than target.
#
# AppKit. One idle coordinator lives on the host view. After the timeout it dims a black
# layer above the game surface and below the pointer, and the first input afterwards wakes
# it and is consumed instead of delivered. Activity arrives from every source the host
# already sees - direct touch, presses, hover, clicks, the on-screen trackpad - plus the two
# it cannot see, which the app reports through one notification: a controller button, and the
# controller touchpad relay. Nothing here hooks UIApplication sendEvent:, changes brightness,
# idleTimerDisabled, the session, game memory or game settings.
#
# Applies after: 0064-controller-touchpad-mouse-handoff-test.patch
# Applies to: translation/Metal/Presentation.m, translation/AppKit/AppKit.m
# Upstream: product-specific.
#
